From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: set BPI-R4 Pro lan5 LED function

The integrated PHY0 LED is wired to the yellow activity LED of the
R4 Pro lan5 port. Give it the standard LAN function so the LED class
name is complete and OpenWrt can bind its netdev trigger reliably.

The yellow color and lan5 role come from the accepted Linux R4 Pro
description. The LAN function is corroborated by tested OpenWrt PR
discussion and the standard MT7988 integrated-PHY LED binding.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dtsi       | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dtsi
@@ -288,6 +288,7 @@
 
 &gsw_phy0_led0 {
 	color = <LED_COLOR_ID_YELLOW>;
+	function = LED_FUNCTION_LAN;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
